codex
Depth 40 exposed the exact mismatch: the outer summary existentially forgot final `j`, while `scan-finish` correctly requires `j = N`. I’m strengthening the outer invariant, not the answer: `outer-one-ahead` always performs an iteration, and `outer-one-past` is guarded so an already-finished state must already have `j = N`. Both may then preserve the true final binding exactly.
apply patch
