codex
The bounded target revealed the real continuation mismatch: each phase helper matched only when its source statements were the entire `Stmts` item. Inside `minPath`, those statements have a syntactic tail, so the helper never fired and the semantics expanded every branch. I’m changing the three helpers to bind and reproduce `TAIL:Stmts` explicitly; this is valid for all tails because these phases contain no `return`, and it preserves the subsequent `Return(result)` exactly.
apply patch
