codex
The narrowed simplifier reduced growth but did not remove it, so the remaining cause is the overly broad generic loop claim: its wildcard scope/heap frame can match at many unrelated control points. I’m replacing the five overlapping result helpers with one exact target-frame, generalized mid-loop claim. It still proves the loop inductively over symbolic `R` and prefix `A`, but its continuation and entire call frame are exact, so its circularity can match only the intended back edge.
apply patch
