codex
The phase wrapper’s generalized postcondition is causing the cross-claim implication to be explored instead of discharged. The wrapper does not need to be generalized—the loop claim already is. I’m narrowing only the wrapper to the exact target boundary: empty prefix and `pairs = k // 2`. That makes its postcondition byte-for-byte the full target postcondition while leaving the inductive loop claim fully symbolic.
apply patch
