codex
The guard-head theorem is sound and self-proving, but its theorem consequence still does not subsume the outer target state. I’m switching the same exact invariant to the operational body/back-edge state—the semantics’ natural positive-branch cut. Then the full target splits normally: the positive branch uses that claim at `resultBody`, while the zero branch executes the odd tail and return directly. This is the standard one-iteration reachability shape and eliminates the wrapper entirely.
