codex
The head-form residual caught a real footprint issue: for negative `R`, the loop exits without writing `pairs`, so a summary claiming `pairs = 0` is too strong. I’m restricting this loop claim to its true positive invariant (`R > 0`). The `R = 1` branch executes to `pairs = 0`; larger `R` uses the same circularity. The target’s zero-iteration case remains operational and unsummarized.
apply patch
